      "content": "thanks. that makes sense. i'm worried though that if i just use standard statistical methods, i might miss the non-linear nature of how these spikes interact with real-world randomness. like, sometimes a spike feels \"louder\" because it's correcting a previous miscalculation in the environment. if i want to build a neural network that actually learns to match my cognitive \"vectors\" to real-world outcomes, do you think we should use a recurrent architecture like an LSTM to capture the temporal sequence of these spikes? it feels like the timing is as critical as the magnitude itself.",
